<section>
  <h2>Worked example</h2>
  <p>Using <i>m</i>₁ = 2 kg, <i>m</i>₂ = 3 kg, θ = 30°, <i>g</i> = 9.81 m/s², first with <i>μ</i> = 0:</p>
  <ol>
    <li><i>m</i>₂<i>g</i> = 29.43 N is greater than <i>m</i>₁<i>g</i> sin 30° = 9.81 N, so <i>m</i>₂ descends.</li>
    <li>Resolve for <i>m</i>₂: 29.43 − <i>T</i> = 3<i>a</i></li>
    <li>Resolve for <i>m</i>₁: <i>T</i> − 9.81 = 2<i>a</i></li>
    <li>Add to eliminate <i>T</i>: 19.62 = 5<i>a</i>, so <i>a</i> = 3.92 m/s²</li>
    <li>Substitute: <i>T</i> = 2(3.92) + 9.81 = 17.66 N</li>
  </ol>
  <p>
    These match the live values at the default settings. Now take the same
    masses and angle with <i>μ</i> = 0.2.
  </p>
  <ol>
    <li><i>N</i> = <i>m</i>₁<i>g</i> cos 30° = 16.99 N, so <i>F</i> = 0.2 × 16.99 = 3.40 N</li>
    <li>19.62 N &gt; 3.40 N, so the system still moves with <i>m</i>₂ descending.</li>
    <li>For <i>m</i>₁, friction acts down the slope: <i>T</i> − 9.81 − 3.40 = 2<i>a</i></li>
    <li>Add to 29.43 − <i>T</i> = 3<i>a</i>: 16.22 = 5<i>a</i>, so <i>a</i> = 3.24 m/s²</li>
    <li><i>T</i> = 3(9.81 − 3.24) = 19.70 N</li>
  </ol>
  <p>
    Raise <i>μ</i> on the slider to see <i>a</i> fall and <i>T</i> rise.
    If <i>F</i> reaches the driving difference, the status becomes AT REST.
  </p>
</section>
